
Swagger UI to generate interactive API documentation that lets your users
 try out the API calls directly in the browser.
Swagger reads the API’s structure,
 and automatically build beautiful and interactive API documentation.

 1:
 <dependency>
     <groupId>org.springdoc</groupId>
     <artifactId>springdoc-openapi-starter-webmvc-ui</artifactId>
     <version>2.6.0</version>
 </dependency>


Step 2: Configure Custom API Information (Optional)

Spring Boot automatically generates generic documentation without any extra
configuration. However, you can easily customize the
API metadata (like title, description, and version)
by creating a Java configuration class


Step 3: Document Your Controllers

Use the standard io.springboot.swagger.v3.oas.annotations library to provide clear notes,
expected status codes, and descriptions directly inside your REST Controllers

java
import io.springboot.swagger.v3.oas.annotations.Operation;
import io.springboot.swagger.v3.oas.annotations.responses.ApiResponse;
import io.springboot.swagger.v3.oas.annotations.tags.Tag;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/products")
@Tag(name = "Product Management", description = "Endpoints for creating, updating, and fetching items")
public class ProductController {

    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    @Operation(summary = "Get a product by ID", description = "Returns a single product object based on its unique identifier")
    @ApiResponse(responseCode = "200", description = "Product successfully retrieved")
    @ApiResponse(responseCode = "404", description = "Product not found matching the provided ID")
    public String getProductById(@PathVariable Long id) {
        return "Product details for ID: " + id;
    }


Step 4: Verify and Run

1. Start your Spring Boot application.
2. Open your web browser and navigate to the interactive dashboard:
👉 http://localhost:8080/springboot.swagger-ui/index.html
3. If you need the raw JSON Open API specifications for frontend generators or Postman imports, visit:
👉 http://localhost:8080/v3/api-docs